  "conditions": "Spring has sprung in the Tetons and Rendezvous Mountain holds all the secrets to unlock the goods. From high country corn cycles in the morning, to afternoon cruisers in the soft stuff, one thing is for sure, your goggle tan has never looked so good! Look for clear and sunny skies today with calm to moderate winds trending out of the West at 9-12 MPH, afternoon gusts will range from 15-20 MPH. Mountain temperatures will reach the upper 30's at the top Tram dock, while the valley floor will be basking in the mid to upper 50's after lunch. Celebrate skiing in the springtime, as mountain-wide conditions soften up throughout the day and the gentle giant continues to ski well. Stay safe out there and stay stoked in the sunshine! -MB",
